; `def` is not allowed inside a proof block, like `use`: `let x` / `def k iff P x` used to give
; `∀ x (k iff P x)`, and then `P d` from `P c` (soundness review of 2026-09-29, §8.17)
load logic
bool P
arity P 1
const P, c, d
show (P c) implies (P d)
proof
    let x
        def k iff P x
;;; EvalError: `def` is not allowed inside `let`
